<concept id="t00551">
	<title>Manual set speed change</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e03552">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03553">
								<image href="images/N_SP327_C00_037.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<fig id="e03554">
								<image href="images/N_SP327_C00_038.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>When the Manual Assist menu or Speed Limit Assist is selected, if the road speed limit changes while Manual Speed Limit Assist or Smart Cruise Control is operating, an up or down arrow is displayed to indicate that the set speed needs to be adjusted. You can change the set speed according to the speed limit by using the (<image align="left" href="images/WKIA_334.jpg" scale="15" placement="inline"/>) or (<image align="left" href="images/WKIA_335.jpg" scale="15" placement="inline"/>) switch on the steering wheel.</p>
		<p>The set speed adjustment operates under the following condition:</p>
		<ul id="e03555">
			<li>
				<p>On roads with a speed limit of 30 km/h (20 mph) or higher.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</conbody>
